<title>POLAND: NBP sells PLN 750 mln of 91-day, 182-day bills.</title>
<headline>NBP sells PLN 750 mln of 91-day, 182-day bills.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Poland sold a total of 750 million zlotys worth of its 91-day and 182-day bills at a tender for Polish money market dealers, the NBP said.</p>
<p>The average yield of the shorter paper eased to 22.18 percent from 22.20 percent at the last tender while the average yield of the 182-day bills stayed flat at 22.00 percent.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
